    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d683">

                <pb facs="0653" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.9315 Manchuria/231: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-11T20:00:00+09:00">June 11, 1940—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 11—1:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>436. Our 435, June 11, 7 p.m.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d683-f1"/> Soviet-Japanese
                    agreement concerning delimitation of Manchurian-Outer Mongolia border near
                    Nomonhan. A member of the Foreign Office has informed us in addition to
                    confirming the report of the agreement, that it was merely initialed by Molotov
                    and Ambassador Togo at Moscow and must now be referred to the Mongolian and
                    Manchurian Governments for their <pb facs="0654" n="642" xml:id="pg642"/>
                    approval. He anticipated no difficulty in this respect, however, and added that
                    the Soviet Union has been adamant about the necessity of settling this border
                    issue before proceeding to take up other outstanding problems such as the
                    conclusion of a long term fisheries agreement and Russian interference with
                    Japanese interests in Soviet Sakhalin. The Japanese press although pleased
                    emphasizes that the settlement of the Nomonhan question constitutes only one of
                    the many problems confronting the two countries.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
